---
import PolicyPage from "../components/PolicyPage.astro";
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Shipping Policy"
  description="Check Cocoa & Kind delivery areas, shipping fees, and order timing before purchasing."
  kicker="A little note about delivery"
>
  <p>
    We want every box to arrive in lovely condition. The details below must be completed to
    match the shop's real delivery service before this page is used to accept orders.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Delivery-method estimate</h2>
  <p>
    We calculate approximate straight-line distance between the shop location and the delivery
    pin provided at checkout. At or within a 15 km radius, the order is marked
    <strong>Porter — manual booking</strong>. Beyond 15 km, it is marked
    <strong>courier — manual booking</strong>. This is a preliminary suggestion, not a booking,
    delivery promise, or road-distance calculation. We check the address and arrange the
    appropriate available service manually.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Where we deliver</h2>
  <p>
    Dispatch location: <strong>[ADD CITY AND STATE]</strong>. Delivery is available to:
    <strong>[LIST STATES, PIN CODES, OR SERVICE AREA]</strong>. Areas we cannot currently serve:
    <strong>[LIST EXCLUSIONS, OR SAY NONE IF ACCURATE]</strong>. Contact
    <strong>[ADD CUSTOMER SUPPORT PHONE OR EMAIL]</strong> to confirm your address if you are
    unsure. Do not accept an order for an address that has not been confirmed serviceable.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Shipping fee — required before taking payment</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      The current Razorpay checkout charges the chocolate subtotal only; it does not calculate or
      collect shipping. Do not accept live payments until the actual shipping fee is included in
      the amount shown to the customer before payment.
    </strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Set out the real delivery fee or rate by area or order, any free-delivery threshold, and
    whether taxes or handling are included: <strong>[ADD SHIPPING CHARGES AND ANY CONDITIONS]</strong>.
    Never add an undisclosed delivery charge after payment. If a parcel cannot be sent for the
    paid amount, contact the customer and follow the published cancellation and refund policy
    before proceeding.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Preparation and delivery estimates</h2>
  <p>
    Order preparation time: <strong>[ADD NUMBER OF BUSINESS DAYS]</strong>. Estimated transit
    time by service area: <strong>[ADD DELIVERY ESTIMATES]</strong>. Orders are handed to the
    delivery provider after payment and address confirmation. State cut-off times, weekend or
    holiday handling, and how customers receive tracking information:
    <strong>[ADD DISPATCH, HOLIDAY, AND TRACKING DETAILS]</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Estimates are not guaranteed arrival dates. Tell customers how to contact the shop about a
    delayed parcel: <strong>[ADD DELAY AND LOST-PARCEL PROCESS]</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Chocolate care and delivery issues</h2>
  <p>
    Add how the products are packed and any verified temperature or weather limitations:
    <strong>[ADD ACTUAL CHOCOLATE PACKAGING, STORAGE, AND WARM-WEATHER DELIVERY DETAILS]</strong>.
    Please provide a complete, accessible delivery address and phone number. Explain what
    happens when a delivery attempt fails, an address is incorrect, or a parcel arrives damaged,
    incorrect, or incomplete: <strong>[ADD REDELIVERY AND DELIVERY-ISSUE PROCESS]</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cancellation and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    For cancellation, returns, refunds, or replacement requests, use the process and contact
    details in the shop's <a href="../terms-and-conditions/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>:
    <strong>[ADD LINKED, COMPLETE CANCELLATION AND REFUND TERMS BEFORE LAUNCH]</strong>. Customer
    rights required by law continue to apply.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Delivery and address enquiries: <strong>[ADD CUSTOMER SUPPORT EMAIL AND PHONE]</strong>.
    Effective date: <strong>[ADD EFFECTIVE DATE]</strong>.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
